7.6.1.2
log
@gfortran 11.1.0 now compares the argument list in all calls to the same
subroutine or function that occur anywhere in a source file.  A compilation
error results if any arguments do not match in rank (scalar, vector, array,
etc.).  The error can be downgraded to a warning with -std=legacy, but such
warnings can only be suppressed by inhibiting ALL warnings.  This annoying
behaviour makes it necessary for the subroutine or function calls to match,
or at least appear so.  This affected one call to WCSGTI in relation to the
VALUE argument.
@
